            <ArticleTitle>Angioplasty at coronary bifurcations: single-guide, two-wire technique.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>57-63</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A technique is described for angioplasty at coronary bifurcations. This simple approach utilizes a single guiding catheter, an exchange wire, and a conventional dilatation catheter and guidewire. With this &quot;protective&quot; guidewire technique, side branches at risk from occlusion during dilatation of a primary coronary segment can be protected and dilated secondarily; continual access to the threatened side branch is maintained with a &quot;standby&quot; exchange wire in the branch vessel.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
